{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he awoke, etc., and behold, it was a dream.</b> Perhaps it is because in the dream of the ears he did not recognize, while dreaming, that he was dreaming, but thought he was awake, due to the great clarity of the matter, and he perceived it without confusion as a dreamer does. Rather, only after he rose from his sleep did he recognize in retrospect that he had been dreaming. And this is what the verse says — <b>and Pharaoh awoke</b>, and behold, he found himself that the matters had been a dream and not while awake:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:24.381362051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}